// E0444: a `.plyx` built by a different binary.
//
// The header carries `blake3(FRONTEND_VERSION)`, `blake3(RUNTIME_VERSION)` and
// `BODY_ENCODING`, and a run refuses an artifact that disagrees with any of the
// three before it decodes a body:
//
//   $ ply-0.12 build artifact_version.ply -o app.plyx
//   $ ply-0.13 run app.plyx
//   E0444  this artifact was built under BODY_ENCODING 6 and this binary reads 7
//          = rebuild it with `ply build`
//
// Its own code and not `E0443` because the responses are opposite: a version
// mismatch is rebuilt, a corrupt transfer is re-sent. Telling a deployment to
// re-transfer a file that will never verify is how an incident lasts an hour.
//
// `ply_std::digest()` is the one header field whose mismatch is **not** an
// error. A stdlib definition is content-addressed like any other, so a differing
// digest over modules this program never imported is a fact rather than a fault,
// and it is reported `W0605 STDLIB_CHANGED` while the run proceeds.

pub fn shade(n: Int) -> Int = n + n

fn main() -> Int = shade(21)
